  "file": "src/git/repos.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A branch name has more than 30 pull requests on GitHub. Recovery sees only the first 30, so it can miss the run's recorded PR and try to open a new one, or miss a second PR with the same head commit and fail to notice the ambiguity. The discreet allocator only hands out branch names that have no PRs, so getting past 30 on one name is very unlikely.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: the 30-item truncation is gh's own default page size and needs real GitHub or a gh that paginates; the code below shows no --limit and no pagination",
   "evidence": "repos.ts:1594-1597 `gh pr list --repo <slug> --head <branch> --state all --json url,headRefOid` has no --limit, so gh returns at most 30. lookupUrl (l.1529-1537) treats the array as complete: when a PR URL is recorded it matches `pr.url === identity.prUrl`, and it raises 'several pull requests share head' only for matches inside that window. The deliver() lookup in engine.ts does the same. At base the `.[0].url` lookup had the same truncation, but this change adds identity and uniqueness decisions on top of the truncated list."
  },
  "B": {
