   "failure_scenario": "Recovery encounters more than 30 pull requests matching the same branch filter. It can accept an apparently unique match while another is hidden, or miss its recorded pull request and attempt to create a replacement.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "gh pr list --help; bun test \"$TMPDIR/adjudicate-693-head.test.ts\"",
    "output": "Local gh help: `-L, --limit int Maximum number of items to fetch (default 30)`.\nA fake gh modeled 31 branch-matching PRs, with matching SHAs at positions 1 and 31: F3 {\"totalPRs\":31,\"selected\":\"https://github.com/test/repo/pull/1\",\"recorded\":\"https://github.com/test/repo/pull/31\",\"recovered\":null,\"created\":\"https://github.com/test/repo/pull/32\"}.\nCaptured calls included `pr list --repo test/repo --head change/add-farewell --state all --json url,headRefOid` and then `pr create --repo test/repo --head change/add-farewell --base main --title Farewell --body-file -`. No network was used."
   },
   "evidence": "At head, `prLookup` uses `gh pr list ... --head branch --state all` without pagination or a completeness check. `lookupUrl` rejects ambiguity only when `matches.length > 1` within the returned list; a recorded URL absent from that list yields an empty result and permits creation. The threshold concerns 31 PRs matching the branch filter, not merely 31 repository PRs. Base already used the limited list, but selected its first URL; the new identity-based recovery and discreet branch naming expose the incomplete-list assumption as a false uniqueness/absence decision."
